    "narrative": "The LawDog lineup is heavily leveraged against favorable matchups today, with **Bryce Harper** (74.59) and **Lawrence Butler** (72.30) leading the charge. Both benefit significantly from facing Junk, whose 4.51 xERA provides a soft landing for our top-tier bats. **Bryce Harper** is the clear anchor of the day; his combination of prime cleanup-adjacent positioning and a strong xwOBA profile makes him the premier start. Meanwhile, **Lawrence Butler** continues his recent surge, capitalizing on a dynamic platoon advantage that pushes his efficiency score well into the elite tier. **Jonathan Aranda** (66.40) and **Luis Arraez** (64.92) round out our high-floor contingent, both benefiting from favorable matchups against Young and Junk, respectively.\n\nWhile our starters are well-positioned, the bench decision for **Gavin Sheets** (40.99) was the most difficult. He was the final player squeezed out by our strict efficiency threshold; while he faces a reasonable matchup, his negative park and pitcher skill modifiers against McLean made him less attractive than the rest of the cohort. We are also keeping a close eye on **Masyn Winn**, who provides sneaky value today despite hitting lower in the order. His score of 60.12 is buoyed by his elite sprint speed and a \"Slow SP Delivery\" tag against Lowder, which significantly increases our probability of securing those scarce stolen bases. \n\nRisk management remains a priority given our game cap strategy. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Braden Montgomery** (44.51), who faces the toughest test of the day against the formidable Imanaga (3.74 xERA). His inclusion is a strategic hedge on his switch-hitting versatility, but he remains firmly in the \"marginal\" start category. We are otherwise healthy, though with **Cal Raleigh**, **Will Smith**, and **Daulton Varsho** unavailable due to off-days or injury, the margin for error in our utility slots remains thin. The objective remains clear: maximize the production of our primary hitters against the mid-rotation arms while leaning on **Masyn Winn** and **Justin Crawford** to keep our SB pace competitive.",
